<title>CHINA: CHESTERFIELD YR NET LOSS HK$14.998 MLN.</title>
<headline>CHESTERFIELD YR NET LOSS HK$14.998 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	  1.0 loss    vs 5.1 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)   nil	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 2.98 loss   vs 54.36 loss</p>
<p>    Net			   14.998 loss vs 65.926 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		    102.85	vs 94.15</p>
<p>    Company name		Chesterfield Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		 September 16-22</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	  N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Chesterfield is a property investment and food manufacturing concern.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one 1999 warrant for 10 shares held. The warrants will be entitled to exercise their rights to subscribe at an initial subscription price of HK$0.45 per share, subject to adjustment in accordance with the terms and conditions set out in the warrant instrument, expected to be on or around September 22, 1997, and ending on September 30, 1999.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss mainly on provision for loss on disposal of listed investments.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
